# Jira tickets on pull requests

When the change is tied to a Jira issue, the GitHub PR must name that issue.

A PR is related if the user cited a key (`NOP-3`), the branch or commits contain one, or the work implements a ticket from this chat. Do not invent a key.

## Title

Prefix the existing title shape with the key in brackets:

`[NOP-3] Orders: reject refund when payment is pending`

Not `Orders: reject refund when payment is pending` with the key only in the body.

## Body

Put a markdown browse link near the top (before What changed):

`Jira: [NOP-3](https://<site>.atlassian.net/browse/NOP-3)`

Use the project's real browse URL. Do not paste issue descriptions, comments, or customer data.

## Unrelated work

If there is no ticket, keep the normal title. Do not add a fake key or an empty Jira heading.
